ills in the 4th–5th centuries CE, primarily during the Vishnukundina dynasty era.","summarySource":"wikipedia","wikipediaTitle":"Undavalli Caves","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/40/Undavalli_Caves_-_Copy.JPG","thumb":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/40/Undavalli_Caves_-_Copy.JPG","w":1200,"h":686,"author":"NikhilSvp","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Undavalli_Caves_-_Copy.JPG"}},{"id":"vijayawada_kanaka_durga_temple","areaId":"vijayawada","name":"Kanaka Durga Temple","category":"monument","tags":["history","photo"],"location":{"lat":16.5154,"lng":80.6059},"visitMinutes":45,"priceLevel":0,"photoSeed":"vijayawada_kanaka_durga_temple","tickets":[{"vendor":"Official","url":"http://www.indrakeeladri.org/","official":true}],"signals":{"commonsDepicts":0,"commonsNearby":15,"wikiPageviews":3834,"wikidataSitelinks":11,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-22"},"hashtags":["kanakadurgatemple","vijayawada"],"hours":{"week":[{"open":"09:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"09:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"09:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"09:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"09:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"09:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"09:00","close":"18:00"}],"note":"Typical hours — check the official site"},"summary":"Kanaka Durga Temple, officially known as Sri Durga Malleswara Swamyvarla Devasthanam, is a Hindu temple dedicated to Kanaka Durga. The deity in this temple is also popularly referred as Kanaka Durga. The temple is located in Vijayawada, Andhra Pradesh, India on the Indrakeeladri hill on the banks of Krishna River.","summarySource":"wikipedia","wikipediaTitle":"Kanaka Durga Temple","photo":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Kanakadurga_Temple_gopuram.jpg/1280px-Kanakadurga_Temple_gopuram.jpg","thumb":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Kanakadurga_Temple_gopuram.jpg/500px-Kanakadurga_Temple_gopuram.jpg","w":1200,"h":900,"author":"Srikar Kashyap","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kanakadurga_Temple_gopuram.jpg"}},{"id":"vijayawada_statue_of_social_justice","areaId":"vijayawada","name":"Statue of Social Justice","category":"monument","tags":["art","photo"],"location":{"lat":16.50722,"lng":80.63151},"visitMinutes":20,"priceLevel":0,"photoSeed":"vijayawada_statue_of_social_justice","tickets":[],"signals":{"commonsDepicts":5,"commonsNearby":48,"wikiPageviews":952,"wikidataSitelinks":6,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-22"},"hashtags":["statueofsocialjustice","vijayawada"],"bestLight":"morning","summary":"The Statue of Social Justice also known as the Dr. B. R. Ambedkar Smriti Vanam, is a 206-ft tall statue located in Vijayawada in the Indian state of Andhra Pradesh. The memorial dedicated to B. R. Ambedkar, an Indian polymath, statesman, social reformer and the father of the Indian Constitution.","summarySource":"wikipedia","wikipediaTitle":"Statue of Social Justice","photo":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cc/Statue_of_Social_Justice%2C_At_night.jpg/1280px-Statue_of_Social_Justice%2C_At_night.jpg","thumb":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cc/Statue_of_Social_Justice%2C_At_night.jpg/500px-Statue_of_Social_Justice%2C_At_night.jpg","w":1200,"h":1600,"author":"Mr Nerd 96","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Statue_of_Social_Justice,_At_night.jpg"}},{"id":"vijayawada_mogalrajapuram_caves","areaId":"vijayawada","name":"Mogalrajapuram Caves","category":"monument","tags":["history","photo"],"location":{"lat":16.50611,"lng":80.64694},"visitMinutes":45,"priceLevel":0,"photoSeed":"vijayawada_mogalrajapuram_caves","tickets":[],"signals":{"commonsDepicts":1,"commonsNearby":63,"wikiPageviews":274,"wikidataSitelinks":8,"fetchedAt":"20