um, located at M. G. Road of Vijayawada. It was renamed in the memory of the renowned film director, illustrator, cartoonist and author Bapu.","summarySource":"wikipedia","wikipediaTitle":"Bapu Museum, Vijayawada","photo":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/44/Bapu_museum_18.jpg/1280px-Bapu_museum_18.jpg","thumb":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/44/Bapu_museum_18.jpg/500px-Bapu_museum_18.jpg","w":1200,"h":675,"author":"Koushik","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bapu_museum_18.jpg"}},{"id":"vijayawada_akkanna_madanna_caves","areaId":"vijayawada","name":"Akkanna Madanna Caves","category":"monument","tags":["history","photo"],"location":{"lat":16.51389,"lng":80.60667},"visitMinutes":45,"priceLevel":0,"photoSeed":"vijayawada_akkanna_madanna_caves","tickets":[],"signals":{"commonsDepicts":2,"commonsNearby":33,"wikiPageviews":282,"wikidataSitelinks":6,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-22"},"hashtags":["akkannamadannacaves","vijayawada"],"hours":{"week":[{"open":"09:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"09:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"09:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"09:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"09:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"09:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"09:00","close":"18:00"}],"note":"Typical hours — check the official site"},"summary":"Akkanna Madanna caves are a group of rock-cut Hindu cave temples in Vijayawada, Andhra Pradesh, India. Dated to mid 7th-century and dedicated to Shiva, they were excavated by the Eastern Chalukya dynasty. They consist of the upper (larger) and lower caves.","summarySource":"wikipedia","wikipediaTitle":"Akkanna Madanna Caves","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/b9/Akkanna_Madanna_Rock_cut_Caves%2C_Vijayawada_city.jpg","thumb":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/b9/Akkanna_Madanna_Rock_cut_Caves%2C_Vijayawada_city.jpg","w":1200,"h":750,"author":"Adityamadhav83","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Akkanna_Madanna_Rock_cut_Caves,_Vijayawada_city.jpg"}},{"id":"vijayawada_indira_gandhi_stadium","areaId":"vijayawada","name":"Indira Gandhi Stadium","category":"other","tags":["family"],"location":{"lat":16.50485,"lng":80.63793},"visitMinutes":90,"priceLevel":2,"photoSeed":"vijayawada_indira_gandhi_stadium","tickets":[],"signals":{"commonsDepicts":4,"commonsNearby":49,"wikiPageviews":218,"wikidataSitelinks":6,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-22"},"hashtags":["indiragandhistadium","vijayawada"],"summary":"Indira Gandhi Stadium is located in Vijayawada city of the Indian state of Andhra Pradesh. The stadium has hosted a solitary ODI between India and West Indies on Sunday, 24 November 2002. It also hosted a WODI in December 1997 between England women and Pakistan women, which was won by England by 230 runs.","summarySource":"wikipedia","wikipediaTitle":"Indira Gandhi Stadium (Vijayawada)","photo":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e6/Aerial_view_of_Indira_Gandhi_Stadium_during_35th_Vijayawada_Book_Festival.jpg/1280px-Aerial_view_of_Indira_Gandhi_Stadium_during_35th_Vijayawada_Book_Festival.jpg","thumb":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e6/Aerial_view_of_Indira_Gandhi_Stadium_during_35th_Vijayawada_Book_Festival.jpg/500px-Aerial_view_of_Indira_Gandhi_Stadium_during_35th_Vijayawada_Book_Festival.jpg","w":1200,"h":675,"author":"Saiphani02","license":"CC BY 4.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Aerial_view_of_Indira_Gandhi_Stadium_during_35th_Vijayawada_Book_Festival.jpg"}},{"id":"vijayawada_wv_rajiv_gandhi_park","areaId":"vijayawada","name":"Rajiv Gandhi Park","category":"park","tags":["nature","photo"],"location":{"lat":16.50921,"lng":80.61222},"visitMinutes":60,"priceLevel":0,"photoSeed":"vijayawada_wv_rajiv_gandhi_park","tickets":[],"signals":{"commonsNearby":3,"wikidataSitelinks":0,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-22"},"hashtags":["rajivgandhipark","vijayawada"],"bestLight":"golden","summary":"Created by the Vijayawada Municipal Corporation with great care, this park is at the entrance of the city and features an impressive horticultural network. It also has a mini zoo and a musical water fountain.","summarySource":"wikivoyage","wikivoyageTitle":"Vijayawada","photo":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2d/Prakasham_Barrage_from_Vijayawada_5.jpg/1280px-Prakasham_Barrage_from_Vijayawada_5.jpg","thumb":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2d/Prakasham_Barrage_from_Vijayawada_5.jpg/500px-Prakasham_Barrage_from_Vijayawada_5.jpg","w":1200,"h":541,"author":"PJeganathan","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Prakasham_Barrage_from_Vijayawada_5.jpg"}},{"id":"vijayawada_bhavani_island","areaId":"vijayawada","name":"Bhavani Island","category":"landmark","tags":["photo"],"location":{"lat":16.5263,"lng":80.5698},"visitMinutes":60,"priceLevel":1,"photoSeed":"vijayawada_bhavani_island","tickets":[],"signals":{"commonsDepicts":0,"commonsNearby":0,"wikidataSitelinks":0,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-22"},"hashtags":["bhavaniisland","vijayawada"],"summary":"Bhavani Island is on Krishna River close to the city. AP Tourism is converting this 133-acre (54-hectare) island into a tourist spot and a river-front resort. The island offers some cottages to stay in and some adventure and fun sports. The journey to the island by boat is very pleasant.","summarySource":"wikivoyage","wikivoyageTitle":"Vijayawada","photo":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Bhavani_Island.jpg/1280px-Bhavani_Island.jpg","thumb":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Bhavani_Island.jpg/500px-Bhavani_Island.jpg","w":1200,"h":900,"author":"Vin09","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","lice